From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:10:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 256/342] realtekwifi: RTL8822BU, phase 1 (bring-up and
 scanning)

A new chip in rtwn for RTL8822BU adapters (sold as RTL8812BU/RTL8822BU,
AC1200/AC1300): power-on sequences, firmware download through the
reserved pages and DDMA, queue and FIFO setup, the BB/AGC/RF tables with
their RFE conditions, 20/40/80 MHz channel switching on 2.4 and 5 GHz,
Tx power, Tx/Rx descriptors and PHY status, and the wifi-only coex
setup. The RTL8822B code and tables are derived from Linux's rtw88
(v7.0) under its BSD-3-Clause option (LICENSE.rtw88).

rtwn core: optional sc_fw_download and sc_dma_init hooks, and on USB an
endpoint mapping hook and a flag for Tx descriptors without the OWN bit;
other chips are unchanged. 36 USB IDs from rtw88's rtw8822bu.c.

Compile-tested only: association, firmware rate adaptation, IQK and
power save come in the next phases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
