+/*
+ * RTL8822B Tx descriptor setup.
+ *
+ * Management and control frames follow rtw_tx_mgmt_pkt_info_update():
+ * QSEL_MGMT, driver rate without fallback, hardware sequence number
+ * (EN_HWSEQ + DISQSELSEQ, HW_SSN_SEL = port).  Data frames follow
+ * rtw_tx_data_pkt_info_update() for QSEL (TID), A-MPDU and RTS fields,
+ * but take the rate from rtwn/net80211 (USE_RATE) because firmware rate
+ * adaptation is not set up yet (TODO phase 2: H2C_CMD_RA_INFO, then
+ * leave USE_RATE clear for unicast data when sc_ratectl is
+ * RTWN_RATECTL_FW).
+ *
+ * The USB checksum (rtw8822b_fill_txdesc_checksum(): XOR of the first 32
+ * bytes into dword 7) and the packet size/offset are filled in by
+ * rtwn_usb_tx_start(); rtwn_usb_tx_start() must not set an OWN bit for
+ * this chip (dword 0 bit 31 is DISQSELSEQ), see rtwn_usb_softc.tx_no_own.
+ *
+ * Sources (rtw88 v7.0): tx.h / tx.c (struct rtw_tx_desc,
+ * rtw_tx_fill_tx_desc, rtw_tx_pkt_info_update,
+ * rtw_tx_mgmt_pkt_info_update, rtw_tx_data_pkt_info_update,
+ * rtw_tx_pkt_info_update_rate, rtw_tx_rsvd_page_pkt_info_update,
+ * get_tx_ampdu_factor), main.c (get_rate_id).
+ */
+
