+/*
+ * RTL8822B tx power: per-rate power index = efuse base (per channel
+ * group, bandwidth and stream count) + min(by-rate offset, regulatory
+ * limit), written to the TXAGC registers (0x1d00 / 0x1d80).
+ *
+ * This is rtw88's full computation with these differences:
+ *  - only the worldwide (RTW_REGD_WW) limits are kept, i.e. the lowest
+ *    limit of all regulatory domains in the table; rtw88 selects the
+ *    domain from the country (rtw_regd_get()).
+ *  - no SAR limits (rtw88 without SAR configuration: max_power_index).
+ *  - no power tracking remnant (always 0 on the 8822B).
+ *  - only the rate sections the 8822B writes (CCK .. VHT 2SS).
+ *  - the result is clamped to 0 as well as to max_power_index.
+ *  - an unprogrammed (0xff) efuse base index is replaced by a
+ *    conservative default.
+ *
+ * Sources (rtw88 v7.0): phy.c (rtw_get_channel_group,
+ * rtw_phy_get_2g_tx_power_index, rtw_phy_get_5g_tx_power_index,
+ * rtw_phy_rate_to_rate_section, rtw_phy_get_tx_power_limit,
+ * rtw_get_tx_power_params, rtw_phy_get_tx_power_index,
+ * rtw_phy_set_tx_power_level*, rtw_phy_get_rate_values_of_txpwr_by_rate,
+ * rtw_phy_store_tx_power_by_rate, rtw_parse_tbl_bb_pg,
+ * rtw_channel_to_idx, rtw_phy_set_tx_power_limit, rtw_xref_*,
+ * rtw_parse_tbl_txpwr_lmt, rtw_phy_tx_power_by_rate_config,
+ * rtw_phy_tx_power_limit_config, rtw_phy_init_tx_power), rtw8822b.c
+ * (rtw8822b_set_tx_power_index, rtw8822b_set_tx_power_index_by_rate).
+ */
+
